cycling, aka gaining and losing weight,
which can actually be more detrimental

00:33:42.130 --> 00:33:46.630
to health than just maintaining their
original weight. I will also say that a

00:33:46.630 --> 00:33:52.360
lot of people do not have the ability and
capacity to work out two to three times

00:33:52.360 --> 00:33:59.410
a day like John or maintain a very kind
of simplified macro focused diet. Having

00:33:59.410 --> 00:34:03.520
said that, the main message that John
consistently delivers on this channel

00:34:03.520 --> 00:34:08.860
when it comes to weight loss is to do so
in a healthy and sustainable way. He also

00:34:08.860 --> 00:34:12.640
completely discourages extreme behaviors
like restrictive dieting and over

00:34:12.640 --> 00:34:17.320
exercising as a means to reach weight
loss goals which I do appreciate him

00:34:17.320 --> 00:34:21.700
saying. In a lot of his videos, he does
talk about how you can't lose weight

00:34:21.700 --> 00:34:26.950
from a place of "I hate my body" and
expect those changes to last. Which, again,

00:34:26.950 --> 00:34:32.530
I can 100% agree with. I admire what John
has been able to achieve for himself

00:34:32.530 --> 00:34:36.040
through his lifestyle changes and
appreciate the balanced messaging that

00:34:36.040 --> 00:34:40.060
he provides for his viewers. John also
does differentiate between being

00:34:40.060 --> 00:34:45.310
overweight and being morbidly obese, as
in one video he mentions that he does

00:34:45.310 --> 00:34:50.170
believe you can be overweight and
metabolically healthy which is actually

00:34:50.170 --> 00:34:54.550
supported by ample scientific evidence
but he also is concerned about

00:34:54.550 --> 00:34:59.920
glamourizing the extreme end of the
spectrum aka morbid obesity. Now I do

00:34:59.920 --> 00:35:04.690
agree with John that this is murky
territory because I can appreciate the

00:35:04.690 --> 00:35:08.979
potential health implications of being
morbidly obese, while I can also

00:35:08.979 --> 00:35:13.749
appreciate the risks of weight cycling.
So I see it as a bit of a risk-benefit

00:35:13.749 --> 00:35:18.549
analysis that is really unique to the
individual. I myself have had to do a lot

00:35:18.549 --> 00:35:21.999
of research and just a lot of
soul-searching and I've shared my

00:35:21.999 --> 00:35:26.200
updated thoughts on weight loss and HAES
on my channel so you can check that out

00:35:26.200 --> 00:35:30.400
right here if you want to know where I
stand and how I support people's goals

00:35:30.400 --> 00:35:34.930
no matter what they are. Now while John
might be really vocal about denouncing

00:35:34.930 --> 00:35:38.829
the body-positive
or fat acceptance movement, and I've become

00:35:38.829 --> 00:35:42.910
a little bit more moderate or neutral in
my views at this point on this, I do

00:35:42.910 --> 00:35:47.709
appreciate that when he does discuss
influencers who promote HAES or body

00:35:47.709 --> 00:35:53.410
positivity he does so in a relatively
respective way. In one video where he was

00:35:53.410 --> 00:35:57.999
discussing Sophie Hagen's Instagram post
about celebrating world obesity day, he

00:35:57.999 --> 00:36:02.709
says that while he may not believe that
celebrating obesity as a concept is

00:36:02.709 --> 00:36:07.869
healthy he doesn't ever judge an
individual or think negatively about the

00:36:07.869 --> 00:36:11.199
individual. Rather he points out that he
doesn't really think we should be

00:36:11.199 --> 00:36:15.999
celebrating a person for being obese the
same way that he doesn't think we should

00:36:15.999 --> 00:36:20.949
be celebrating a person for being fit.
There are just more interesting and

00:36:20.949 --> 00:36:25.180
important attributes to a person other
than the size of pants that they wear. I

00:36:25.180 --> 00:36:28.630
also like that he says that his weight
loss didn't make him a better person

00:36:28.630 --> 00:36:33.670
than somebody who is still 600 pounds,
rather the only thing that has changed

00:36:33.670 --> 00:36:39.579
was that he thinks he is now healthier
and that is awesome for him. I mean I

00:36:39.579 --> 00:36:43.449
agree with all of that. I guess where I
get a little turned off, hence why I'm

00:36:43.449 --> 00:36:48.099
bringing this all up to you guys, is that
I find he does talk about obesity and

00:36:48.099 --> 00:36:54.880
others experiences of obesity in a less
than sensitive way which, again, is kind of

00:36:54.880 --> 00:36:58.839
his schtick. He's all about why are we
all being so offended by everything but

00:36:58.839 --> 00:37:04.449
as an example I've heard him say things
like eat yourself to death which yeah

00:37:04.449 --> 00:37:09.699
seems pretty assumptive and insensitive.
There isn't a whole lot of consideration

00:37:09.699 --> 00:37:12.480
for socioeconomic factors, mental health,

00:37:12.480 --> 00:37:17.610
medication, and other physical ailments.
I mean his assumption is just that

00:37:17.610 --> 00:37:23.280
someone is a size that they are solely
for eating too much and that may have

00:37:23.280 --> 00:37:27.270
been the case for him, I don't know, and
it may be the case for a lot of other

00:37:27.270 --> 00:37:32.190
people. But I don't think that we can
make assumptions about why or how

00:37:32.190 --> 00:37:36.480
someone is the size that they are, so I'm
not saying that the information on his

00:37:36.480 --> 00:37:42.570
channel is problematic per se but it may
be stigmatizing and triggering and

00:37:42.570 --> 00:37:48.450
therefore problematic to a lot of my
viewers, so that is what I'm here to flag.

00:37:48.450 --> 00:37:53.190
Now are there any good takeaways from
the obese to beast's channel? Definitely.

00:37:53.190 --> 00:37:56.730
I think we can all take something away
from his channel especially when it

00:37:56.730 --> 00:38:02.070
comes to his philosophy around food and
keeping things simple and sustainable.

00:38:02.070 --> 00:38:07.800
This is so key when it comes to eating. I
mean you can try every diet on the planet,

00:38:07.800 --> 00:38:12.900
but what it really comes down to is
whether or not you enjoy it and if it's

00:38:12.900 --> 00:38:17.520
sustainable for you. We also see John's
openness to switching up his routine and

00:38:17.520 --> 00:38:22.440
adding more value to his way of eating. I
think it can definitely be very easy for

00:38:22.440 --> 00:38:26.550
some of us to kind of get stuck in a
routine pattern of eating, so I am glad

00:38:26.550 --> 00:38:30.780
to see that we're able to kind of take
this journey with him. I'm also a big

00:38:30.780 --> 00:38:35.370
lover of super simple food hacks and his
"no fuss" approach to eating and cooking

00:38:35.370 --> 00:38:40.020
which I definitely think is a really
great takeaway for me, personally. Bottom

00:38:40.020 --> 00:38:44.850
line, I really enjoyed John's content and
I think he's actually a really smart guy.

00:38:44.850 --> 00:38:50.160
I also enjoyed how real he is on his
channel and his "no-fuss" positive

00:38:50.160 --> 00:38:54.150
attitude when it comes to food. While
he's not a nutrition professional, per se,

00:38:54.150 --> 00:38:59.220
he doesn't seem to promote any dangerous
fad diets and while I may not agree with

00:38:59.220 --> 00:39:03.930
all of his statements, I can fully
respect his personal experience and his

00:39:03.930 --> 00:39:07.860
opinion. Well folks, that is all for
today's video. Thank you again to audible

00:39:07.860 --> 00:39:12.030
for sponsoring this video! If you liked
it be sure to give it the thumbs up,

00:39:12.030 --> 00:39:15.770
leave me a comment below with who you
would like to see me review next,

00:39:15.770 --> 00:39:21.890
subscribe to the channel, and I'll see
you next time on Abbey's Kitchen. Bye!

